  "profileHelpDialogTitle": "Help & Support",
  "profileHelpDialogBody": "Door selection\nChoose an accessible target from Profile > Quick Access Door. You can clear the selection or refresh the list. If the list is empty, ask your administrator to check your access permissions.\n\nUsing QR codes\nCamera permission is needed only for scanning. If permission is denied, check camera access in device settings. Show your personal QR code to a supported reader and refresh it when expired. Scanning an identity label alone does not create a passage record.\n\nRecords and access issues\nCheck your connection and refresh the relevant screen. A door command, a physical passage and an official attendance result are different events. Contact your personnel or system administrator about missing or incorrect records.\n\nSupport details\nGive your administrator the app version (About the App), the time of the issue and the displayed error. Do not share passwords, session information or your personal QR code.",
  "profilePrivacyDialogTitle": "Privacy information",
  "profilePrivacyDialogBody": "App data information — 19 October 2026\n\nNGS Plus retrieves and displays your organization’s employee details, accessible devices and your access events from the service. Personal QR codes are obtained from the service; the camera is used for scanning. A door request sends the selected target to the service. Theme, language and scoped target preferences are stored on this device.\n\nYour organization manages employee details, access permissions and event records. Contact your personnel or data administrator about processing purposes, retention periods, legal basis and personal data requests.\n\nThis explanation describes app data use and does not replace your organization’s approved privacy policy. A published organization policy link is not configured in this version.",
